well it's better than son of Batman  Justice League throne of Atlantis I  can't exactly say I was excited to go  into this thing because the track record  for the DC animated movies so far based  off the new 52 their whole new  continuity that they're building not  been great we had Justice League war  which was very uneven start and then it  immediately took a nosedive with son of  Batman which was terrible but let's  start positive on this thing most of the  stuff that worked in Justice League war  still works here primarily the action  the action is very well staged it is  fairly regularly paced it's a little bit  bloodier than I think it needs to be and  it feels a bit more gratuitous this time  than it did in Justice League war not  quite as bad as son of Batman was but it  seems unnecessary like when I see one of  the superheroes take down an enemy I'm  fine with them just punching the guy and  he drops I don't need him to be cut in  half and blood spray everywhere maybe I  just grew out of that I don't know but  the actress still pretty good although I  can't give this movie quite the same  pass on that basis that I gave to  Justice League war because while the  action is good I don't like that this  appears to very clearly be an action  franchise now I mean the older DC  animated movies they always had action  but I never would have described them as  action movies with a one or two  exceptions for the most part you just  wouldn't love them as that you wouldn't  sell them to somebody as it's an action  movie these that's kind of what they are  is kind of what they've all been and I'm  not loving that as a general trend but  again the action is good  there's no sore spots on the voice cast  this time and then there were some  pretty big ones when we dealt with son  of Batman so that's a nice improvement  again Bob out on par with what we got  with Justice League Wars now they've  have won fairly big improvement which is  Wonder Woman because in Justice League  war she was so bad I use grinding my  teeth every time she was on thankfully  that's been largely corrected because  first of all they recast I feel a little  bit bad because I think Michelle  Monaghan's delivery in Justice League  war was probably the fault of the  writers and the director they didn't  replace her with rosario Dawson who  gives a bit more of that stoic strength  that I like and expect from Wonder Woman  which is also an indicated that they're  now writing her properly as opposed to  the ridiculous stupid fish-out-of-water  jokes they were using her for in Justice  League war so massive improvement for  her  there was another casting replacement  they recast the voice for Green Lantern  now it's now Nathan Fillion which is not  a bad thing I'd like Nathan Fillion I  like him as Green Lantern the thing is  though there was nothing wrong with the  guy who they had doing Green Lantern in  Justice League war you know they fix  something that wasn't broken so that  that struck me as a little odd most of  the new blood is pretty soft and really  the big focus here is on Arthur curry  aka Aquaman this is at the heart of it  his story and his stories handled fairly  well for the most part  unfortunately this really would have  been a much better movie if it wasn't a  Justice League movie because the two  don't really cross paths for a while I  mean the Justice League is kind of aware  that there's something going on under  the sea and they're looking into that  and Arthur curry is dealing with his own  personal issues and sort of coming to a  realization of who he is and how he's  torn between two worlds the Justice  League factors and very peripherally to  that and then the thing as it hit its  climax really started to fall apart I'll  come back to that in a bit if they're  gonna remain so rigid to this 75 minute  runtime they really needed to drop the  rest of the Justice League out of this  and just make it an Aquaman movie I feel  like we could have gotten a better depth  and better impact out of Aquaman's side  of the story because there's a lot of  stuff in there that feels like there's a  lot more to this story than you're  giving us particularly in terms of  Atlantis and the backstory of the royal  family that's already in place Aquaman's  mother and his half-brother and there's  a struggle going there you feel that  there's history but the movie does not  have the time to delve in in anything  more than a surface level where this  really falls down is in orem who is the  primary villain he's just incredibly  one-dimensional now he should be a  pretty deep villain because you think  about it he has lived in Atlanta sees  pure Atlantean he has a right to the  throne but his mother she would rather  have his half-brother who has never even  lived in Atlantis and knows nothing  about it take the throne rather than him  I mean that's a legitimate gripe for  somebody to have he's like you're gonna  bring in this guy who you didn't raise  you know virtually nothing about you're  gonna let him sit on the throne whether  I've lived with these people and I know  this world there's real drama to be  mined from that but they make him so  over-the-top evil and they just push it  too far then it just it doesn't have the  impact that the setup could have really  brought and I also need to point out  because I mentioned that really the  climax is where things start to fall  apart and where the film pretty much  lost me completely was as we went into  the final climactic fight now I'll put a  spoiler warning up on this but I don't  think I'm ruining any surprises I mean  that of course it ends in a big fight  they all end in big fights firstly or  himself is really dumb but he's got to  be the worst military tactician in the  history of ever because the way that he  begins his assault on the surface world  is with a massive tidal wave and the  Justice League sees this thing coming  and they know it's gonna hit all up and  down the East Coast primarily the focus  on metropolis naturally so this thing is  approaching metropolis and they say flat  out we can't stop that they're not gonna  be able to save everybody and the title  wave comes up to the city and stops it  stops dead parts like a curtain and  there's arms army why would you have a  title wave come up just to hide your  army and not have the title way to  actually hit the city and do a bunch of  damage that's like dropping a bomb but  when the bomb lands it doesn't explode  it opens up and there's your fighting  squad and they just come out and you  know what coming back to the violence  the film really causes a problem for  itself when it comes to the climactic  battle because you know when they take  on the Atlantean army they are killing  them left and right now that kind of  eases off about midway through the  battle and I figured out why at the end  because Arthur is going to take down arm  and he is going to assume command and he  is now the ruler of Atlantis and  suddenly you know these aren't the  enemies anymore these are our allies but  you shoot yourself in the foot doing  that when only about 10 minutes ago we  were watching them get killed left and  right but suddenly you can't help but go  how many people who thought they were  fighting to defend their  nation did our heroes just slaughter man  this reviews gotten weird on me because  I started off saying it was not that  patent now I've spent so much time  ripping into it look it's not great I'm  certainly not gonna say is great I  hesitate honestly to even say that it's  good it is better than son of Batman son  of Batman just aggravated me from  beginning to end this one started out  fine started out okay but it then it  just went downhill and it never  recovered but it just it makes me not  excited for the movies that are in this  continuity never at this point the only  stuff I'm gonna be looking forward to  anymore is the stuff that is separate  from this continuity like assault on  Arkham was so yes I'm just gonna throw  my feelers out there I personally feel  that the caliber of films that have been  coming out this new continuity based on  the new 52 is just as a whole several  notches down from pretty much the entire  lineup of films that were being done  prior the more standalone stuff do you  think that's the case do you think it's  about the same or do you think that  these are actually better than what we  used to be getting whatever it is drop  something on comets and let's talk about  it as for me I'll be back as soon as I  can get my next fix

